   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kyrgyzstan: (GHS) Enhancing the One Health approach in Kyrgyzstan and its capacity to control zoonotic diseases</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations (FAOs) assistance to the Republic of Kyrgyzstan the Global Health Security Program (GHSP) is to support animal health capacity building for the prevention, early detection, and response to animal and public health threats, particularly zoonoses, and antimicrobial resistance (AMR), strengthening and operationalizing a One Health approach. Findings and recommendations from capacity assessments will be considered when preparing the detailed implementation plan. There are eight priority diseases, identified by the country, four of them are zoonoses (anthrax, brucellosis, echinococcosis, and rabies).</narrative>
  </description>
